  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Outcome</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved road transport services in the project areas</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">A 10% increase per annum in freight and passenger traffic on the project roads for 3 years after project completion. 
Progress/Status: Traffic volumes  were more than four times higher in 2012 than in 2005. Mazar-e-Sharif to Dar-i-Suf (2005 traffic count 891; 2012 traffic count 4,466). Bamyan to Yakawlang (2005 traffic count 266; 2012 traffic count 1,766). 
Data Source: Statistics compiled by the Ministry of Public Works;
Socioeconomic surveys 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="100" year="2012"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2015-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2015-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="70"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">A 20% decrease in freight and passenger transport fares passing through the project roads within 1 year of project completion 
Progress/Status: Freight transport fares reduced from AF2.2/kg to AF1.2/kg (45%) in the Bamyan to Yakawlang region. Bus fares decreased by 80%. 
Data Source: Statistics compiled by the Ministry of Public Works;
Socioeconomic surveys 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="100" year="2012"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2013-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2013-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="80"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">A 50% decrease in travel time on the project roads for all types of vehicles immediately after project completion 
Progress/Status: Average of 75% decrease in travel time per trip over the entire project road in good weather. 
Data Source: Statistics compiled by the Ministry of Public Works;
Socioeconomic surveys 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="100" year="2012"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2013-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2013-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="50"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 4</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">An average 30% reduction in travel time to the nearest health, primary education, and other essential services from the project areas within 3 months of project completion 
Progress/Status: Travel times in the project area had been reduced by 75% by project completion. 
Data Source: Statistics compiled by the Ministry of Public Works;
Socioeconomic surveys 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="100" year="2012"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2013-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2013-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="70"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
